+# Mario Kart World (0400C3F00006E000): the rewriter's patches of this game's own builds. dm/tools/patch_nso.py loads every profile's patches.py and applies those of a module's NSO build ID.
+CUTS = {
+  # nxkit (fps30.patch): a steady 30 fps. The framework's frame function (main+0x3a9e28) hands framework +0x214, the interval of the frame, to nvnWindowSetPresentInterval (main+0x3aa0a0), and it
+  # is what the frame's step follows (added to the frame counter at main+0x3a9fb8). Framework +0x210 chooses how the next interval is found (main+0x3a9ec8): 0 is dynamic, from the time the frames
+  # took, between 1 and 2, as the game runs on its own (54 changes of pacing in log 27, each an uneven stretch); 1 and 2 are fixed (main+0x3aa034). The cut reads it as 2, the game's own fixed 30 fps
+  # path, so the game's speed stays right; the host follows, and after a second at interval 2 its display link runs at 30 Hz (nvn_game_fps)
+  '9e244438c3d8ef1c703a6a85ef99c4f0': [
+    (0x3a9ec8, '681242b9', '48008052', 'fixed present interval 2, 30 fps: ldr w8,[x19,#0x210] -> mov w8,#2'),
+    # nxkit: no texture compaction. agl::TextureDataMgr's per-frame update (main+0x523ca4) sends its "aglTextureDataMgr::Compaction" thread (body main+0xe2c028) message 100 each frame, and that thread
+    # moves texture data inside the 2.4 GB texture heap (main+0x4f96a8: memcpy, up to megabytes at a time, seen copying 3.5 MB in log.prev(14)). On a console that is RAM to RAM. Here the guest
+    # memory is a file on an 8 GB phone: the source is mostly out on flash, so each move reads it back and dirties new pages, and each moved texture is a new texture to upload (log.prev(14): 25-50 MB/s of
+    # page-ins, 150,000 write-protection faults, 17,000 first uploads in five minutes, 39 of 48 stalls with threads stopped in page faults). Without the message the heap's state stays 3, its idle
+    # state from the constructor (main+0xccf404), which the update's low-memory path needs (main+0x523d54). What it can cost: a fragmented heap in a long session, where the game's retry thread takes over
+    (0x523d00, '88010034', '0c000014', 'no compaction: cbz w8,#0x523d30 -> b #0x523d30, message 100 is never sent'),
+  ],
+}
